# Review: CodeGraphPlugin

The plugin is substantially built. The dev-server route (`CodeIndexMiddleware`) runs `code-index mcp` as a child,
refuses non-loopback, foreign-host, non-JSON and cross-origin callers, and is tested against a fake MCP server. The
client names the missing route on a 404. The graph model (dedupe, needed boxes, removal), the illustrator layout
with per-package frames, the command filter and the 40-box budget all have unit tests. Weak spots are the UI and the
operation handlers: no test drives an operation handler, the 300-box `LimitError`, dragging, double-click or the
details panel's actions, and no automated test runs the assistant scenario.

The spec's fences are malformed, so the review parser sees only the first declaration of each fenced block: `Node`,
`Edge`, `NodeKind`, `Layout`, eight of the nine ops, four of the five components and scenario `T-2` are not listed
as items, and `F-5` and scenarios `T-3`-`T-5` sit outside any fence. This review judges the 19 items the parser
lists. For the unlisted F-5 work: `Command.run`, `Filter`, `Budget`, `Grounding` and the `CommandBar` with
Whistle speech exist, and `Command.test.ts` covers the turn loop.

Of 19 items: 7 done, 9 untested, 2 partial, 0 diverged, 1 missing.

